WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.099 --> 00:00:06.149
Manulife Financial Corporation is a Canadian
insurance company and financial services provider,

00:00:06.149 --> 00:00:09.250
with a head office in Toronto, Canada.

00:00:09.250 --> 00:00:14.200
The company operates in Canada and Asia as
"Manulife Financial" and in the United States

00:00:14.200 --> 00:00:16.820
primarily through its John Hancock division.

00:00:16.820 --> 00:00:22.320
It is one of the largest life insurance companies
in the world by market capitalization, and

00:00:22.320 --> 00:00:26.130
has approximately 84,000 employees.

00:00:26.130 --> 00:00:31.720
Manulife Bank of Canada is a wholly owned
subsidiary of Manulife Financial Corporation.

00:00:31.720 --> 00:00:33.319
History

00:00:33.319 --> 00:00:36.809
Private stock company
The firm was founded as The Manufacturers

00:00:36.809 --> 00:00:40.010
Life Insurance Company in 1887.

00:00:40.010 --> 00:00:46.059
Its first president was Sir John A. Macdonald,
the first Prime Minister of Canada.

00:00:46.059 --> 00:00:51.679
The company sold its first policy outside
of Canada in Bermuda in 1893.

00:00:51.679 --> 00:00:59.520
In 1894, policies were sold in Grenada, Jamaica
and Barbados; Trinidad and Tobago, and Haiti

00:00:59.520 --> 00:01:07.579
in 1895; and British Honduras, British Guiana,
China and Hong Kong in 1897.

00:01:07.579 --> 00:01:13.869
In 1901, Manulife amalgamated with the Temperance
and General Life Assurance Company, a Toronto-based

00:01:13.869 --> 00:01:19.310
Canadian life insurer that provided preferred
rates to abstainers of alcohol.

00:01:19.310 --> 00:01:23.990
Manulife continued to offer abstainers rates
into the 1920s.

00:01:23.990 --> 00:01:29.640
In 1931, it opened its first southern China
branch in British Hong Kong.

00:01:29.640 --> 00:01:34.530
Shortly thereafter, it established itself
as a leading life insurer in the region with

00:01:34.530 --> 00:01:38.399
branches in Macau, Shantou and Amoy.

00:01:38.399 --> 00:01:42.700
Mutual company
In 1958, shareholders voted to change its

00:01:42.700 --> 00:01:48.030
legal form from a joint stock company to a
mutual organization, making the company privately

00:01:48.030 --> 00:01:50.749
owned by its policyholders.

00:01:50.749 --> 00:01:57.319
In 1996, the company entered an agreement
with the Zhong Hong Life Insurance Co. Ltd.,

00:01:57.319 --> 00:02:06.189
based in Shanghai, to form China’s first
joint venture life insurance company, Manulife-Sinochem.

00:02:06.189 --> 00:02:12.690
In 1984, Manulife announced that it had acquired
Waterloo, Ontario-based Dominion Life Assurance

00:02:12.690 --> 00:02:17.600
Company: a deal that included the purchase
of all of the outstanding stock of the company

00:02:17.600 --> 00:02:19.720
from Lincoln National.

00:02:19.720 --> 00:02:25.430
Dominion Life was founded in Waterloo in 1889,
and Manulife made a commitment to the community

00:02:25.430 --> 00:02:28.860
to retain a significant presence in Waterloo.

00:02:28.860 --> 00:02:35.110
In 1988, Manulife opened a new five-storey
office building at 500 King St. North in Waterloo

00:02:35.110 --> 00:02:37.830
to house its Canadian Division.

00:02:37.830 --> 00:02:43.470
In 1996, the company entered an agreement
with Sinochem to form Shanghai -based Zhong

00:02:43.470 --> 00:02:51.600
Hong Life Insurance Co. Ltd., China’s first
joint venture life insurance company, and

00:02:51.600 --> 00:02:56.680
was granted a license that made it the second
foreign insurer to be allowed re-entry into

00:02:56.680 --> 00:02:57.680
China.

00:02:57.680 --> 00:03:03.870
Demutualization and public company
In 1999, its voting eligible policyholders

00:03:03.870 --> 00:03:09.140
approved demutualization, and the shares of
Manulife Financial Corporation, the holding

00:03:09.140 --> 00:03:14.240
company of The Manufacturers Life Insurance
Company and its subsidiaries, began trading

00:03:14.240 --> 00:03:19.720
on The Toronto Stock Exchange, the New York
Stock Exchange and the Philippine Stock Exchange

00:03:19.720 --> 00:03:31.090
under the ticker 'MFC', and on The Stock Exchange
of Hong Kong under the ticker ‘945’.

00:03:31.090 --> 00:03:35.360
In 2002, Manulife–Sinochem Life Insurance
Co. Ltd. was granted approval by the China

00:03:35.360 --> 00:03:40.870
Insurance Regulatory Commission to open a
branch office in Guangzhou, China, the first

00:03:40.870 --> 00:03:47.010
branch license granted to a foreign invested
joint–venture life insurance company.

00:03:47.010 --> 00:03:52.970
In 2003, Manulife-Sinochem received approval
for a branch office in Beijing, the first

00:03:52.970 --> 00:03:59.130
multiple-branch license granted to a foreign-invested
joint venture life insurance company.

00:03:59.130 --> 00:04:03.450
The firm is now licensed to operate in more
than 50 Chinese cities.

00:04:03.450 --> 00:04:10.650
In 2003, Manulife Financial Corporation and
John Hancock Financial Services, Inc. announced

00:04:10.650 --> 00:04:17.310
a tax–free stock–for–stock merger of
the companies, creating a global insurance

00:04:17.310 --> 00:04:18.920
franchise.

00:04:18.920 --> 00:04:24.880
Completed in April 2004, the merger created
the largest life insurer in Canada, second

00:04:24.880 --> 00:04:30.090
largest in North America, and fifth largest
in the world at the time.

00:04:30.090 --> 00:04:37.660
In 2013 Richard DeWolfe became the Chair of
the company’s board, succeeding Gail Cook-Bennett,

00:04:37.660 --> 00:04:41.390
who retired after serving 34 years on the
board.

00:04:41.390 --> 00:04:48.950
In 2009, Donald Guloien, the Chief Investment
Officer, succeeded Dominic D’Alessandro

00:04:48.950 --> 00:04:52.910
as President and CEO of the company.

00:04:52.910 --> 00:05:00.810
Shortly before his departure, D’Alessandro
modified his retirement package; the restricted

00:05:00.810 --> 00:05:07.200
units would only vest for a total of $10 million
if the shares reached $36 by the end of 2011,

00:05:07.200 --> 00:05:11.750
and he would receive $5 million if the shares
hit $30.

00:05:11.750 --> 00:05:18.030
This was in response to shareholders’ reaction
to the first quarterly loss ever posted by

00:05:18.030 --> 00:05:20.630
the firm in its public history.

00:05:20.630 --> 00:05:25.520
Under Guloien's leadership, the first initiatives
were a dividend cut and an equity offering

00:05:25.520 --> 00:05:30.250
to bolster Manulife's capital levels, making
it difficult for the share price to reach

00:05:30.250 --> 00:05:33.240
the target levels needed to vest.

00:05:33.240 --> 00:05:41.840
In September 2009, the company purchased AIC’s
Canadian retail investment fund business.

00:05:41.840 --> 00:05:48.590
In October 2009, it purchased Pottruff &amp; Smith
Travel Insurance Brokers Inc., a Canadian

00:05:48.590 --> 00:05:52.850
broker and third party administrator of travel
insurance.

00:05:52.850 --> 00:06:01.210
In 2010, the company announced that it had
purchased Fortis Bank SA/NV’s1 49 per cent

00:06:01.210 --> 00:06:05.910
ownership in ABN AMRO TEDA Fund Management
Co. Ltd.

00:06:05.910 --> 00:06:12.680
The new joint venture, Manulife TEDA Fund
Management Company Ltd., provides traditional

00:06:12.680 --> 00:06:17.150
retail and institutional asset management
for clients in China.

00:06:17.150 --> 00:06:23.360
The other 51 per cent is owned by Northern
International Trust, part of Tianjin TEDA

00:06:23.360 --> 00:06:25.570
Investment Holding Co., Ltd..

00:06:25.570 --> 00:06:32.210
In June 2012, the company opened Manulife
Cambodia, with headquarters in Phnom Penh.

00:06:32.210 --> 00:06:37.760
In September 2014, Manulife agreed to acquire
the Canadian operations of Standard Life for

00:06:37.760 --> 00:06:41.630
a fee of around $3.7 billion.

00:06:41.630 --> 00:06:46.510
Awards
2013 and 2014 – named to the Dow Jones Sustainability

00:06:46.510 --> 00:06:51.990
North American Index
2013 – The Manulife LPGA Classic received

00:06:51.990 --> 00:06:58.620
the Tournament Owners Association Gold Driver
Award for Charity Promotion, with St. Mary’s

00:06:58.620 --> 00:07:09.510
General Hospital Foundation’s Red Day
2012 and 2013 – named one of Canada’s

00:07:09.510 --> 00:07:17.280
Top Employers for Young People
2010 through 2013 – named one of Canada’s

00:07:17.280 --> 00:07:21.870
Top 100 Employers
2012 – Manulife Investments received the

00:07:21.870 --> 00:07:25.380
Order of Excellence Award from Excellence
Canada

00:07:25.380 --> 00:07:31.910
2012 – President and CEO Donald Guloien
named 2012 International Business Executive

00:07:31.910 --> 00:07:35.770
of the Year
2010 – Manulife Financial recognized on

00:07:35.770 --> 00:07:40.010
the 2010 Investor 500 ranking by Canadian
Business magazine

00:07:40.010 --> 00:07:45.669
2010 – Manulife-Sinochem received an award
of excellence from the State Council National

00:07:45.669 --> 00:07:49.180
Economic Census Commission
Sponsorship

00:07:49.180 --> 00:07:54.580
Manulife Financial was worldwide sponsor for
the 2008 Summer Olympics.

00:07:54.580 --> 00:07:59.240
The sponsorship was acquired along with John
Hancock Financial Services.

00:07:59.240 --> 00:08:06.020
Manulife is the namesake tenant in the tallest
building in Edmonton, Alberta, Manulife Place.

00:08:06.020 --> 00:08:12.070
In 2010, Manulife partnered with Volunteer
Canada and launched its “Get Volunteering”

00:08:12.070 --> 00:08:17.880
platform to provide Canadians with tools to
find volunteer experiences, officially adopting

00:08:17.880 --> 00:08:23.290
volunteerism as the signature cause of its
corporate social investment program.

00:08:23.290 --> 00:08:28.760
Title sponsor of the Manulife Financial LPGA
Classic since 2012.

00:08:28.760 --> 00:08:33.749
Manulife is the parent company of John Hancock
Financial, which has been a principal sponsor

00:08:33.749 --> 00:08:37.689
of the Boston Marathon since 1986.

00:08:37.689 --> 00:08:42.959
Sponsor of Pathways To Education Canada, a
program focused on reducing high school dropout

00:08:42.959 --> 00:08:46.050
rates in low-income communities.

00:08:46.050 --> 00:08:53.750
Manulife Japan is a sponsor of Hoshi General
Hospital’s “Manulife Waku Waku Room”

00:08:53.750 --> 00:08:58.910
project, providing psychological support for
children receiving medical care.

00:08:58.910 --> 00:09:05.240
Title sponsor of the Manulife Walk for Memories,
benefitting the Alzheimer Society of Toronto.

